Here is the definitive automotive lineup for the year 2126. Across the seven prefectures, any vehicle utilizing wheel-less quantum levitation and vector-thrust propulsion is classified as an Aero-Cruiser (or Cruiser).
------------------------------
## 🏛️ Category A: Public & Civilian Use## 1. The Public Commuter (The "Econ-Pod")

* Name: Nimbus-3 Urban Pod
* Purpose: Affordable daily commuting, grocery runs, and basic urban transit for regular citizens.
* Detailed Description: A smooth, egg-shaped capsule made of translucent polymer plastics. The interior is barren, featuring only a bench seat and a central interface globe. It lacks a steering wheel; passengers simply type or speak a destination into the cabin AI. It runs entirely on wireless power beamed from city grid towers.
* Speed Limits: Strictly governed by software to 100 km/h.
* Restrictions: Hard-locked to a maximum altitude of 1.5 meters above the ground. It cannot enter military zones or high-altitude sky-lanes.
* Government Controlled: Yes (Its route and power source are entirely managed by the Municipal Transit Network).
* Disadvantages or Limits: It features zero defensive armor. If the city's wireless power grid fluctuates or goes down, the pod immediately enters an emergency shutdown mode and drops safely but completely dead to the pavement.

## 2. The Public Mass Transit (The "Sky-Bus")

* Name: Strato-Transit Train (Series 9)
* Purpose: Bulk moving of hundreds of civilian workers across heavy industrial city sectors.
* Detailed Description: A massive, multi-segmented, hovering monolithic tube that glides along designated electromagnetic "sky-lanes" suspended between skyscrapers. The exterior is made of utilitarian, unpainted grey titanium plating, while the interior mimics a crowded subway car with standing rails and overhead grab handles.
* Speed Limits: Fixed at a constant 250 km/h on express lines.
* Restrictions: Locked onto a rigid, pre-programmed electromagnetic track network. It cannot alter its course, stop outside of designated stations, or change altitude.
* Government Controlled: Yes (Owned and operated by regional prefectural transport boards).
* Disadvantages or Limits: It is completely unarmored and highly vulnerable to sabotage. If a sky-lane power grid drops, emergency chemical thrusters slowly lower the entire massive vessel to the ground, causing massive traffic blockades.

------------------------------
## 💎 Category B: High Class & Luxury## 3. The High-Class Luxury Cruiser (The "Gilded Wing")

* Name: Helios-9 Sovereign
* Purpose: Ultra-secure, high-status transport for elite corporate executives, politicians, and billionaires.
* Features & Description: A long, sweeping, yacht-like silhouette. The exterior is coated in a "living gold" smart-fluid layer that ripples dynamically in response to changes in ambient sunlight. It features active gravity-dampening cabins, ensuring passengers feel zero bumps or turbulence, even when the vehicle climbs into the upper atmosphere.
* Speed Limits: Capable of Mach 2.0 (approx. 2,450 km/h) at high altitudes.
* Restrictions: Requires a Class-A Private Sky-Lane License. It must clear its flight path with High-Altitude Traffic Control before launching into the upper troposphere.
* Government Controlled: No (Privately owned, but heavily regulated via automated airspace registration protocols).
* Disadvantages or Limits: The active gravity-dampening system and gold smart-fluid skin require immense processing power. If the internal central computer chip gets corrupted or EMP-shocked, the luxury features instantly fail, making the massive vehicle incredibly heavy and difficult to handle manually.

------------------------------
## 🪖 Category C: Military & Tactical## 4. The Military Light Patrol (The "Enforcer")

* Name: Aegis-V Heavy Pursuit Cruiser
* Purpose: Border security, police pursuit, tactical intercept, and rapid troop deployment.
* Detailed Description: Angular, matte-black, and highly intimidating. The chassis is lined with heavy composite armor plating, forward-facing kinetic ramming prows, and EMP-striking headlights designed to shut down fleeing vehicles. The interior is cramped, filled with weapon racks and tactical telemetry screens.
* Speed Limits: Mach 1.5 (approx. 1,830 km/h) with vector thrusters engaged.
* Restrictions: Restricted strictly to military personnel, corporate security forces, and law enforcement. Illegal for civilians to own or operate.
* Government Controlled: Yes (Directly linked to the Central Defence Network; can be remotely overridden or self-destructed by high command).
* Disadvantages or Limits: It is incredibly heavy and loud. When its twin sub-orbital vector thrusters ignite to chase a target, they kick up powerful sonic booms that can shatter nearby civilian building windows and completely drain its dual-core hydrogen engine within three hours of continuous flight.

## 5. The Heavy Combat Juggernaut (The "Tank-Cruiser")

* Name: Atlas-X Overland Titan
* Purpose: Transporting heavy armor, heavy artillery, and bulk military supplies through highly hostile, lawless wasteland territories.
* Detailed Description: A massive, multi-segmented brick of reinforced titanium armor. It hovers on eight separate heavy-duty industrial mag-lev discs that kick up blinding dust storms wherever it travels. It features automated point-defense anti-missile turrets on its roof and a rear deployment ramp for light troops.
* Speed Limits: Maxes out at a slow 90 km/h.
* Restrictions: Military and heavy logistics conglomerate use only. Cannot enter standard civilian city centers due to its massive weight and size damaging road sensors.
* Government Controlled: Yes (Regulated under the Heavy Arms Treaty of 2102).
* Disadvantages or Limits: Its sheer size makes it an incredibly easy target for guerrilla ambushes. Because it is optimized for heavy armor rather than speed, it relies entirely on its automated turret shields to survive incoming rocket fire; if those shields fail, it becomes a sitting duck.

------------------------------
## 🕶️ Category D: Underworld & Syndicate## 6. The Underworld / Mafia Cruiser (The "Viper")

* Name: Obsidian-X Syndicate Executive
* Purpose: Smuggling contraband across prefectural borders, high-value asset protection, and drive-by syndicate hits.
* Detailed Description: A low-slung, sweeping luxury sedan design painted in deep, light-absorbing Vantablack. To a passing police scanner, it registers as a legal, high-class corporate vehicle. However, underneath its frame lies an illegal, military-grade radar-jamming hull plating and hidden, pop-out plasma laser turrets hidden underneath the doors.
* Speed Limits: Officially governed to 150 km/h, but illegally unlocked to hit 450 km/h.
* Restrictions: Banned by federal authorities. Possession of an Obsidian-X with unmapped transponders carries a life sentence in a penal colony.
* Government Controlled: No (Operates entirely off the grid via black-market hardware modifications).
* Disadvantages or Limits: It carries a quick-release fake transponder matrix to spoof legal civilian registration codes. If the spoofing chip burns out mid-transit, the car instantly broadcasts an illegal signature, alerting every military police drone within a 50-kilometer radius.

------------------------------
## 🏁 Category E: Racing & High-Velocity## 7. Pro Factory Race Cruiser (The "Aero-Formula")

* Name: Apex-Formula Mach-1
* Purpose: Corporate-sponsored, high-altitude arena racing and stadium entertainment.
* Detailed Description: A razor-thin needle with massive, adjustable carbon-fiber vector wings. It is designed pure and simple for aerodynamics and downward force. It doesn't hover over roads; it flies through legal, neon-lit ring courses suspended thousands of feet in the air between city skyscrapers.
* Speed Limits: Reaches extreme speeds of up to 800 km/h.
* Restrictions: Allowed only inside sanctioned racing arenas or designated high-altitude training corridors. The driver must wear an advanced pressurized G-suit and use a neural-link system.
* Government Controlled: No (Owned by massive entertainment corporations, but highly regulated by the Global Racing Commission).
* Disadvantages or Limits: Human physical reaction times are too slow to steer it safely; it requires a direct brain-machine interface. If the driver loses focus for a millisecond or experiences a neural lag spike, the vehicle will drift off course and instantly disintegrate against a skyscraper wall.

## 8. Modified Outlaw Race Cruiser (The "Street Scrapper")

* Name: Custom Built "Frankenstein" Strider
* Purpose: High-stakes, illegal underground street racing through abandoned prefectural ruins.
* Detailed Description: Built by hand by stripping down old civilian Nimbus pods or junked military units. They are ugly, loud, and incredibly dangerous—patched together with exposed wiring, unpainted mismatched metal plates, and illegal "over-clocked" civilian thrusters that shoot green or purple plasma flames out of the exhaust ports.
* Speed Limits: Completely variable, but known to push 600 km/h at ground level.
* Restrictions: 100% illegal in all seven prefectures.
* Government Controlled: No (Built and hidden in rogue underground garages).
* Disadvantages or Limits: They completely bypass safety protocols. They have zero altitude locks, meaning drivers can jump over entire buildings, but they are highly unstable. They lack protective force fields or stabilizing AI, meaning they are prone to overheating and exploding mid-race if the engines are pushed too hard.

------------------------------
## ⏳ Category F: The 0.001% Extinction Class## 9. The Old-School Fossil (The "Wheeled Relic")

* Name: 2026 Porsche 911 GT3 RS / 1970 Dodge Charger (Restored)
* Purpose: Ultimate wealth flex, historical preservation, or pure mechanical purism by eccentric collectors.
* Detailed Description: An absolute anomaly in the year 2126. This vehicle has actual rubber tires that touch the actual ground. It runs on a primitive, internal combustion engine that burns liquid petroleum or high-grade alcohol. It features a physical steering wheel, manual gear shifts, three foot-pedals, and makes a deafening, mechanical roaring sound that terrifies modern civilians who have only ever heard the quiet hum of mag-lev tech.
* Speed Limits: Mechanically limited by its old age to around 320 km/h.
* Restrictions: Banned from all automated smart-city highways because it lacks an AI mesh network chip to auto-brake. It can only be legally driven on private estate tracks or unmonitored dirt roads in the deep wasteland ruins.
* Government Controlled: No (Considered a historic artifact rather than a functional vehicle).
* Disadvantages or Limits: Extremely rare and fragile. There are no computer chips, no autopilot, no hovering capability, and no shields. Fuel is practically non-existent and must be synthetically brewed at an extreme cost. If you drive it into a ditch, it crashes physically. In a world of floating pods, it is seen as a beautiful, dangerous, rolling museum piece.

